  "description": "Virginia's 10th Congressional District election will be held on November 3, 2026, to elect the U.S. representative for this Northern Virginia district covering all of Loudoun County, Fauquier County, Rappahannock County, and parts of Prince William and Fairfax counties, as well as the cities of Manassas and Manassas Park. Incumbent Democrat Suhas Subramanyam, first elected in 2024 with 52.3% of the vote, is seeking a second term. The Republican primary on August 4, 2026, features three active candidates—Dave Beckwith, Julie Perry, and Anthony Suttles—after Sam Wong withdrew. Cook Political Report rates the general election as Likely Democratic, reflecting the district's partisan lean (D+6 Cook PVI).",
